# The intermission and the briefing (docs/plans/realm-ui.md, Phase 3): the briefing before a mission
# (MissionBriefing), the debrief after it (MissionComplete) and the finished stele at the end of a
# campaign (CampaignComplete), in each realm's look (ui.realm), and the campaign's flow through
# them, end to end: Home's Campaign starts Campaign I's first mission, whose briefing opens as its
# map loads, the simulation paused (its kicker, name, city and year, image, what's new, threats,
# lead-in, text, goals), ui.layout_issues at 100%, 200% and 75% UI scale in each realm, and Begin,
# which unpauses it. Its island already holds the twenty residents its goal asks for, so it's
# finished at once: the debrief's stele (its title, the line just carved, the rows to come),
# "MISSION 1 COMPLETE", the mission's name, its city and year, the goals table (target, achieved and
# a mark per goal), the stats, the note that its city joins the world map, the layout in each realm
# and scale, Keep playing (the game goes on, the mission stays finished; the Game menu's Mission
# briefing opens the briefing again), then Continue to the world map, whose box offers the next
# mission without a choice ("Begin the mission", which asks in a popup) and starts it, with its
# briefing. Mission 2's town meets its goals too: its debrief, the map, mission 3's briefing. Its
# goals met with world edits and finance.set, its Continue goes to the campaign-complete screen: the
# stele carved in full, the closing line, the missions, the note that Campaign II comes next (coming
# soon), the layout in each realm and scale, and Return to the menu, which shows Kambara's look, the profile
# having reached Campaign II. A hidden test campaign's mission (test_choices) is finished by
# settling a resident: its Continue opens the map's A/B choice, whose site B starts the campaign's
# last mission; finishing that one, Continue goes to the campaign-complete screen. The same flow in
# Kambara's and Tampadesa's own looks, through their hidden test campaigns: briefing, debrief, the
# map's choice (site A, then site B), the last debrief, the finished stele and back to the home
# menu. Last, a choice point started with no site picked offers its two sites in its briefing: one
# begins it there, the other starts its own mission; either is recorded in the profile. The story
# sequences that now play before a briefing and on a debrief's Continue are skipped (Escape) where
# they first play: ui_story.jsonl checks them. Screenshots go to out/ui_intermission/.
#
# Campaign I's missions load the sample saves, so extract them first (unzip saves/sample_saves.zip,
# as CI does). Run it with --fresh-profile, as CI does, at any window size (CI's is 1440 × 800; it
# was checked at 1280 × 720 and 1920 × 1080 too):
#   cargo run -p HeritageBuilder -- --fresh-profile --script crates/game/tests/scenarios/ui_intermission.jsonl
